# JapaneseKeyboard matches unigram rules against each node in a candidate path.
# These rules can promote compound candidates as well as standalone candidates.
# "しろ" was removed because it also promoted "しろ" + "医" etc.
# "したい", "なら", and "ごと" were also withdrawn.
# Do not add "なのか" here: it promoted "馬鹿なのか名" for "ばかなのかな".
# An omission-search candidate can match a word rule despite a different input reading.
